<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Camera preview layout, altered for Android 12.

    ANDROID 12 CHANGE:
    The old version contained a zero-size hidden FrameLayout (surfaceLayout)
    that was used by the OLD Camera1 approach: a 1x1 SurfaceView was injected
    into it via WindowManager.LayoutParams.TYPE_TOAST so the camera could
    render off-screen while the RAT captured frames.

    On Android 12 (API 31) that technique is BROKEN:
      - Overlay window types (TYPE_TOAST / TYPE_PHONE / ...) are restricted.
      - A hidden overlay surface is no longer a valid way to access the camera.
      - Opening the camera from the background requires a FOREGROUND SERVICE
        with foregroundServiceType="camera" (see CameraService.java).

    The rewritten Camera2-based payloads (CameraPreview.java, videoRecorder.java)
    use ImageReader / MediaRecorder.getSurface() and do NOT need any UI surface,
    so this layout is now a plain (empty) container. The id "surfaceLayout" is
    kept so any legacy findViewById(...) does not crash, but it is not used for
    camera rendering anymore.

    Place at: app/src/main/res/layout/camera_preview.xml
    (keep your original filename - the id and structure above are unchanged)
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent">

    <FrameLayout
        android:id="@+id/surfaceLayout"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="match_parent"
        android:background="#000000"
        android:visibility="gone" />

</LinearLayout>

